From e5dd63b3adb13c03efd6691512a0f09449a96490 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 18:45:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] GBA link: fast edge-cycled boot windows, richer detection
 log, per-session log files

Three-session log forensics plus a read of XD's own binary settled how
detection actually works: XD arms its GBA bring-up from the connection
menus and then fires on the next absent->present transition of the
socket, so what it needs from the emulator is frequent fresh boot
windows. Restore the debounced falling-edge auto-reset (window seen this
boot, link continuously down >= 250 ms, >= 1 s between resets; the
250 ms debounce is immune to the RCNT blink race that killed the old
edge trigger, and the 6 s timer stays as a backstop). Config-gated
(GBA/EdgeReset, default on), read once per session so netplay clients
can't diverge mid-run.

Delete the quiet window: it was built to shelter the abandoned bundled
BIOS's cartridge listener and is provably inert in solo (commands at a
down link never reach the core), while adding a rare netplay divergence
surface. Every command is sent again.

Diagnostic log upgrades, all bounded: one file per session named
gba_detect_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.log with the two previous sessions retained
(and shared together by the Android Share button, so a failed
attempt/retry pair arrives intact); 4 MiB budget (the old 1 MiB died
after ~3.5 min of XD's connected-idle RESET polling); JOY-register tap
on the GBA event thread logging SEND-bit transitions with the pending
JOY_TRANS word and attributing each clear to the command that caused it;
JOYSTAT after each command on response lines; response bursts at every
window-open (records which listener answered with what status); a burst
whenever data resumes after >= 1 s of silence (captures the client's
post-hello report with content); ungated rd=/wr= counters in the summary
lines; reason=edge|timer on every auto-reset. On-screen prb counter now
says 65535+ when its 16-bit packing saturates instead of freezing at a
plausible-looking number.
